ak, L. Johannes, F. Perez, and B. Goud. <year>2006</year>. Rab6A and Rab6A' GTPases play non-overlapping roles in membrane trafficking. <source>Traffic.</source> <volume>7</volume>:<fpage>394</fpage>&#x02013;407.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16536738</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib8"><citation citation-type="journal">Du, L.L., and P. Novick. <year>2001</year>. Purification and properties of a GTPase-activating protein for yeast Rab GTPases. <source>Methods Enzymol.</source> <volume>329</volume>:<fpage>91</fpage>&#x02013;99.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11210577</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib9"><citation citation-type="journal">Girod, A., B. Storrie, J.C. Simpson, L. Johannes, B. Goud, L.M. Roberts, J.M. Lord, T. Nilsson, and R. Pepperkok. <year>1999</year>. Evidence for a COP-I-independent transport route from the Golgi complex to the endoplasmic reticulum. <source>Nat. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>1</volume>:<fpage>423</fpage>&#x02013;430.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10559986</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib10"><citation citation-type="journal">Haas, A.K., E. Fuchs, R. Kopajtich, and F.A. Barr. <year>2005</year>. A GTPase-activating protein controls Rab5 function in endocytic trafficking. <source>Nat. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>7</volume>:<fpage>887</fpage>&#x02013;893.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16086013</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><citation citation-type="journal">Hyvola, N., A. Diao, E. McKenzie, A. Skippen, S. Cockcroft, and M. Lowe. <year>2006</year>. Membrane targeting and activation of the Lowe syndrome protein OCRL1 by rab GTPases. <source>EMBO J.</source> <volume>25</volume>:<fpage>3750</fpage>&#x02013;3761.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16902405</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="journal">Johannes, L., and B. Goud. <year>1998</year>. Surfing on a retrograde wave: how does Shiga toxin reach the endoplasmic reticulum? <source>Trends Cell Biol.</source> <volume>8</volume>:<fpage>158</fpage>&#x02013;162.<pub-id